 fee).",price:"$$$$$",address:"Paseo Mujeres, Manzana 1 Supermanzana 3 Cancún, 77400 Cancun, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 313 3716",website:"https://slshotels.com/playa-mujeres/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/sls-playa-mujeres-cancun.webp",photos:[]},{name:"NIZUC Resort & Spa",description:"A tranquil 29-acre secluded sanctuary at Punta Nizuc with private mangroves, protected coral reefs, and reflecting pools. Dedicated kosher kitchens with IKM-certified kosher meals for breakfast, lunch and dinner.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Blvd. Kukulcan Km 21.26, Nizuc, Zona Hotelera, 77500 Cancún, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 891 5700",website:"http://www.nizuc.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/nizuc-resort-spa.webp",photos:[]}],restaurants:[{name:"Ember Kosher Cancun",description:"Upscale Glatt Kosher dining in the Hotel Zone with exceptional ambiance, prime steaks, attentive service, and Mexican specialties (accommodates custom hard-shell and cigar-style tacos).",kosher:!0}],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Cancun",address:"Cancun Convention Center, Blvd. Kukulcan Km 9, Hotel Zone, 77500 Cancún, Q.R.",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Druk",phone:"+52 998 188 6300",website:"http://www.jewishcancun.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Ember Kosher Cancun",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-ember-kosher-cancun.webp",address:"Blvd. Kukulcán Km 8.9, Zona Hotelera, Cancún, Q.R.",kashrus:"KMD (Kosher Maguen David)",phone:"+52 998 217 6216",website:"https://theemberkosher.com",type:"Meat"},{name:"Vico's Grill Kosher Cancun",address:"Blvd. Kukulkan km 8.5, Hotel Zone, Cancún",kashrus:"KMD (Kosher Maguen David)",website:"https://www.vicosgrillkosher.com/",type:"Meat",description:"Kosher steakhouse in the Hotel Zone (beef, chicken, fish and vegetarian dishes)."},{name:"Kosher Italian Gourmet",address:"Blvd. Kukulkan km 8, Plaza Quetzal, Hotel Zone, Cancún",kashrus:"KMD (Kosher Maguen David)",type:"Dairy",description:"Italian kosher restaurant: pizza, pasta and antipasti."}],kosherGroceries:[{name:"Downtown kosher butcher & store",address:"Downtown Cancún (call for address)",description:"A small kosher store and butcher, listed by Chabad of Cancun; phone +52 998 100 0698."},{name:"Chedraui Selecto (Hotel Zone)",address:"Blvd. Kukulkan Km 9, Hotel Zone, Cancún",description:"Supermarket that Chabad of Cancun says carries many kosher products (Chabad keeps a product list)."}],transportation:"City buses (R-1 and R-2) run 24/7 along Blvd. Kukulcán for ~MX$12 cash. Taxis operate on set zone rates throughout the Hotel Zone, but airport taxis are steep (~MX$650 / $38 USD from Punta Cancun to Terminal 3). Uber is approved to operate in Quintana Roo, but taxi unions still clash with app drivers, especially around the airport.",travelTips:["Hotel Zone Public Transit (Buses vs Taxis): Public city buses (routes R-1 and R-2) run up and down Blvd. Kukulcán 24 hours a day for only ~MX$12 in cash. They are safe, air-conditioned, frequent, and significantly more affordable than private hotel taxis for traveling between downtown, Punta Cancún, and southern hotel zone beaches.","Cancun Airport (CUN) Terminal 3 Logistics: The Priority Pass lounge in Terminal 3 (The Lounge) is landside, before the security checkpoint, so visit it before going through security. Note that Mexico does not conduct exit passport control checks when departing on international flights.","Airport Taxi Union Rates: Taxis from Punta Cancun or the Hotel Zone to Cancun Airport Terminal 3 charge steep union-regulated prices (~MX$650 / $38 USD for a <30-minute ride). ADO express buses from downtown Cancun offer a budget alternative for solo travelers.","Punta Cancún Stroll & Luggage Drop: If you have a late afternoon or evening departure, you can arrange luggage drop-off at Chabad of Cancun, spend a relaxing afternoon walking around Punta Cancún and enjoying an early dinner at Ember Kosher, and take a 25-minute taxi directly to CUN Airport.","Punta Cancún Access & Beach Conditions: Punta Cancún (around kilometer 9–9.5) marks the natural bend where the coastline transitions from quiet, wave-protected north-facing waters (Playa Caracol) to breezy eastern surf beaches (Playa Gaviota Azul). The scenic red-and-white Punta Cancún Lighthouse can be reached via a pleasant seaside walk starting from Playa Caracol.","Shabbat & Kosher Meal Planning: Shabbat meal packages should be reserved early in the week with Chabad of Cancun at Plaza Kukulcán (km 13). If staying in northern Punta Cancún resorts, prepare for a ~40-minute walk south along the pedestrian sidewalk or reserve accommodations located within immediate walking distance of Plaza Kukulcán."],nearby:["Isla Mujeres","Playa del Carmen","Puerto Morelos","Riviera Maya"]},{id:"cozumel",businessesAndServicesList:[{name:"Mikvah Mei Malka (Chabad Cozumel)",category:"Mikvah",address:"428 5a Avenida Sur, San Miguel de, COZUMEL, Q.Roo 77600",phone:"+52 987 111 6347",description:"At Chabad Cozumel (mikvah.org also lists it as 'Mai Malka', 5a Av. between Calle 5 & 7, +5219871111985); call to book"}],mikvah:{name:"Mikvah Mei Malka (Chabad Cozumel)",address:"428 5a Avenida Sur, San Miguel de, COZUMEL, Q.Roo 77600"},name:"Cozumel",state:"Quintana Roo",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"/mexca/cozumel__playa-palancar.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 15m",Miami:"1h 50m",Paris:"10h 30m",London:"9h 45m"},weather:"☀️ 83°F",experiences:["Beaches","Wildlife","National Parks"],mustDo:"Snorkeling at Palancar Reef and visiting the Cozumel Chabad Center",description:"A world-class diving destination characterized by breathtaking coral reefs, crystalline waters, and a very popular Jewish traveler community.",bestTimeToVisit:"March to June",nearestAirport:"Cozumel International Airport (CZM)",airportDistance:"2 miles",attractions:[{name:"Palancar Reef",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/c9333b13d02a0c3f.webp",description:"World-renowned marine sanctuary along the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef, celebrated for towering coral pinnacles, deep swim-through caves, and crystal-clear underwater visibility."},{name:"Chankanaab Beach Adventure Park",description:"Adventure park inside Cozumel's National Reef Marine Park with a beach, a lagoon, reef snorkeling and scuba diving, a tropical garden, prehispanic replicas, a Mayan hut and a kids' playground. Some activities, such as dolphin swims, cost extra."},{name:"Punta Sur Ecological Park",description:"Protected ecological reserve at Cozumel's southern tip, home to the historic Celarain lighthouse, crocodile observation towers on Colombia Lagoon, and white-sand beaches."},{name:"Villa Maya Nature Reserve",description:"Lush private ecological reserve nestled in Cozumel’s interior jungle along Camino a Villa Maya, dedicated to rainforest conservation, native biodiversity, and peaceful nature walks."},{name:"Zona Arqueológica San Gervasio",description:"Ancient pre-Columbian Mayan archaeological site on Cozumel, long considered a pilgrimage center dedicated to the goddess Ixchel, with several Mayan structures to explore amid island wildlife."},{name:"Benito Juárez Park (Parque Benito Juárez)",description:"Central waterfront plaza and gathering point in downtown San Miguel de Cozumel, steps from the ferry terminal, with a historic clock tower, a shaded gazebo, a fountain, benches and the colorful COZUMEL sign, surrounded by shops, cafés and restaurants."},{name:"Parque Andrés Quintana Roo (Parque Municipal)",description:"Spacious civic park in Cozumel with a monument to independence figure Andrés Quintana Roo, open-air event pavilions, tree-lined walking areas, spaces where children play, and lively evening gatherings with live music and local island atmosphere."}],activities:[{name:"Scuba Diving at Palancar",description:"Explore deep coral tunnels and marvel at giant sponges and tropical fish."},{name:"Catamaran Sailing & Snorkeling",description:"Sail by catamaran along Cozumel's coast to snorkel at reef sites and visit shallow sandbar areas such as El Cielo, known for its calm, clear waters."}],hotels:[{name:"Casa Mexicana Cozumel",description:"Vibrant, charming waterfront boutique hotel located on the San Miguel malecón with a tranquil oceanfront plunge pool terrace. The absolute top choice for Shabbat-observant travelers on Cozumel due to its short walking distance to Chabad.",price:"$$",address:"Av. Rafael E. Melgar 457, Centro, 77600 San Miguel de Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 987 872 9090",website:"https://casamexicanacozumel.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/casa-mexicana-cozumel-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.6 km (8-minute walk) from Chabad of Cozumel and Alma Kosher on 5a Avenida Sur; Chocolatte and Fuego kosher are within about 0.7 km. Rooms have a small refrigerator. Chabad of Cozumel lists it as a recommended hotel."},{name:"Presidente InterContinental Cozumel Resort & Spa",description:"The premier 5-star luxury resort on the island, boasting an extraordinary private marine reef, secluded ocean coves, and private dive boat pick-up directly from its pier.",price:"$$$$",address:"Carr. Chankanaab Km 6.5, Zona Hotelera Sur, 77600 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 987 872 9500",website:"https://www.ihg.com/intercontinental/hotels/us/en/cozumel/czmha/hoteldetail",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/presidente-intercontinental-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 6 km south of Chabad of Cozumel downtown; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"The Westin Cozumel",description:"Modern, high-rise luxury hotel with magnificent ocean views on Cozumel’s tranquil northern coast, featuring private plunge pool cabanas, rooftop sky lounge, and water sports.",price:"$$$",address:"Carretera Costera Norte Km 4.8, 77613 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 987 872 9200",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/czmwi-the-westin-cozumel/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/the-westin-cozumel-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Rooms have a mini fridge. About 5 km north of Chabad of Cozumel downtown; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Hotel B Cozumel",description:"Boutique oceanfront retreat combining chic Mexican artisanal design with seaside hammocks, an oceanfront hot tub, and direct snorkeling access into a thriving coral lagoon.",price:"$$",address:"Carretera Costera Norte Km 2.5, Zona Hotelera Norte, 77600 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 55 9708 0015",website:"https://www.hotelbcozumel.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/hotel-b-cozumel-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 3 km from Chabad of Cozumel (roughly a 45-minute walk along the coast road, or a short taxi). Rooms have a mini fridge (guest report)."}],restaurants:[{name:"Alma Kosher Restaurant - Cozumel",description:"Popular Glatt Kosher restaurant and grill at the Chabad Center serving fresh fish, burgers, shawarma, and Mexican tacos.",kosher:!0},{name:"Chocolatte Espresso Bar - Kosher",description:"Kosher dairy espresso bar and cafe serving quality coffee, sandwiches, salads, and fresh baked goods under Chabad (popular lunch stop with NY-level pricing).",kosher:!0},{name:"Fuego Restaurant Cozumel",description:"Waterfront kosher dining overlooking the Caribbean ocean, serving steaks and fish; kashrus certified and verified by the Rabbi of Chabad of Cozumel.",kosher:!0}],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of Cozumel",address:"5a Avenida Sur, entre Calle 1 Sur y Adolfo Rosado Salas, Centro, 77668 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Dudi Caplin",phone:"+52 987 104 0770",website:"http://chabadcozumel.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Alma Kosher Restaurant - Cozumel",address:"5a Avenida Sur, C. 1 Sur y, Centro, 77668 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",kashrus:"Chabad of Cozumel (mashgiach temidi; pas Yisrael, chalav Yisrael, Beit Yosef meat)",phone:"+52 987 104 0770",website:"http://chabadcozumel.com",type:"Grill / Mexican Tacos / Fresh Fish",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-alma-kosher-restaurant-cozumel.webp"},{name:"Chocolatte Espresso Bar - Kosher",address:"Calle 1 Sur 58, Centro, Cozumel",kashrus:"American Kosher – Rabbi Dudi Caplin (dairy)",phone:"+52 987 104 0770",website:"http://chabadcozumel.com",type:"Dairy Cafe / Espresso Bar / Sandwiches & Salads"},{name:"Fuego Restaurant Cozumel",website:"https://fuegocozumel.com",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-fuego-cozumel.webp",address:"125 Av. Rafael E. Melgar, between Calle 2 & Calle 4, Cozumel",kashrus:"American Kosher (meat)",phone:"+52 987 871 9770",type:"Waterfront Steaks & Fish / Ocean Views"},{name:"Pita Loca",type:"Fast food",address:"Av. Lic. Benito Juárez 248",kashrus:"Chabad of Cozumel (Rabbi Dudi Kaplin)",description:"Meat fast food (pita)",website:"https://chabadcozumel.com/food/201/"},{name:"Viva Kosher",type:"Catering",address:"10a Avenida Sur 14",kashrus:"Chabad of Cozumel — Rabbi David Nechemia Kaplan (בהשגחת הרב דוד נחמיה כפלין)",description:"Kosher catering, delivery to your address; Chalav Yisrael"}],transportation:"Uber is approved in Quintana Roo and operates in Cozumel. Taxis operate on fixed union zone rates. From Cozumel Airport (CZM), shared shuttles to downtown/Chabad are cheaper than private airport taxis. Scooter and jeep rentals are popular for coastal drives.",travelTips:["Airport Arrival & Shared Shuttles: When arriving at Cozumel International Airport (CZM), skip the expensive private airport taxis and buy a ticket for the shared shuttle at the counter inside the terminal for the quick ride to Chabad of Cozumel or downtown hotels.","Chabad Hospitality & Luggage Drop: Chabad of Cozumel is exceptionally welcoming, staffed by energetic bochurim, and happily accommodates luggage storage for travelers needing a safe place for bags before checking in or heading on a catamaran excursion.","Climate & Passing Showers: Stepping off flights from dry Mexico City into Cozumel brings an immediate wave of tropical Caribbean humidity. Mid-afternoon rain showers occur frequently but typically clear within 10 to 15 minutes.","Interior Transportation: When heading into Cozumel’s interior to visit Villa Maya or San Gervasio ruins, arrange a taxi driver in advance to wait for you or agree on a scheduled return pickup, as cell reception can be spotty and return cabs are rarely available on the highway.","Interior Access Road Closures: The interior transversal roads and connecting unpaved paths leading to inland reserves like Villa Maya and San Gervasio can occasionally close without notice due to private land maintenance, municipal forestry works, or heavy rainfall. Confirm road conditions with your hotel concierge or local drivers prior to departure.","Ferry Logistics from Playa del Carmen: Passenger ferries between Playa del Carmen and San Miguel de Cozumel depart hourly from morning until night, operated alternately by Ultramar and Winjet. Purchase one-way tickets instead of round-trips so you can board whichever ferry leaves next on your return rather than waiting an extra hour for your original company.","Reef-Safe Sunscreen Rule: Cozumel Reefs National Park (Palancar, Colombia), Chankanaab and most cenotes and eco-parks allow only biodegradable (reef-safe) sunscreen. Bring biodegradable sunscreen or wear UV-protective rashguards."],nearby:["Playa del Carmen","Riviera Maya","Punta Sur","San Miguel Centro"],kosherGroceries:[{name:"Chabad Cozumel Kosher Grocery Store",address:"5a Avenida Sur, between Calle 1 Sur and Adolfo Rosado Salas, Centro, San Miguel de Cozumel",description:"Kosher meat (steaks, ground beef, chicken, sausages), cheeses and dairy, snacks, Shabbat and holiday products; Sun–Thu 10 am–10 pm; +52 987 104 0770."},{name:"Chabad Cozumel Bakery",address:"At Chabad of Cozumel, 5a Avenida Sur, Centro, Cozumel",description:"Parve kosher bakery: challahs, breads, cakes and desserts, under Chabad of Cozumel."}]},{id:"playa-del-carmen",businessesAndServicesList:[{name:"Mikvah Playa del Carmen (Chabad)",category:"Mikvah",address:"Calle 10 bis entre ave 25th y 20, Playa del Carmen, Q.Roo 77710",phone:"+52-1-984-156-6811",description:"Chabad of Playa's mikvah: open, by appointment"}],mikvah:{name:"Mikvah Playa del Carmen (Chabad)",address:"Calle 10 bis entre ave 25th y 20, Playa del Carmen, Q.Roo 77710"},name:"Playa del Carmen",state:"Quintana Roo",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/fec3ae65a750d1d6.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 00m (to CUN)",Miami:"1h 45m (to CUN)",Paris:"10h 20m",London:"9h 35m"},weather:"☀️ 83°F",experiences:["Beaches","Waterfalls","Off-Road Adventures"],mustDo:"Strolling down Quinta Avenida and swimming in spectacular cenotes",description:"A chic, trendy coastal resort town on the Riviera Maya, combining beautiful Caribbean coastlines with lively dining, eco-adventure parks, and a welcoming Chabad house.",bestTimeToVisit:"December to April",nearestAirport:"Cancún International Airport (CUN)",airportDistance:"35 miles",attractions:[{name:"Quinta Avenida (5th Avenue)",description:"Lively pedestrian-only street in Playa del Carmen running parallel to the beach for over 4 km, lined with shops, cafes, restaurants, fashion boutiques, art galleries and artisan stalls.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d-quinta-avenida-5th-avenue.webp"},{name:"Cenote Azul",description:"Breathtaking open-air freshwater limestone pool bordered by jungle limestone ledges, crystal-clear turquoise waters, natural cliff-jumping perches, and friendly nibbling fish."},{name:"Cenote Cristalino",description:"Natural cenote near Playa del Carmen with clear water, a cave, and a popular swimming and snorkeling spot."},{name:"Cenote Chaak Tun",description:"Underground cenote cave system near Playa del Carmen featuring stalactites and stalagmites, explored on guided snorkeling tours through low-lit caverns and natural pools."},{name:"Nearby Tulum Archaeological Ruins (Day-Trip)",description:"13th-century walled Mayan city on 12-meter (about 40-foot) cliffs overlooking the turquoise Caribbean Sea, roughly a 45-minute to one-hour drive south of Playa del Carmen."},{name:"Xcaret Park",description:"World-class eco-archaeological theme park celebrating Mexico’s rich folklore, subterranean river swimming, butterfly pavilions, coral aquariums, and the celebrated México Espectacular evening performance."}],activities:[{name:"Cenote Swimming & Diving",description:"Float in the mystical, crystal-clear underground rivers of the Riviera Maya."},{name:"ATV & Zipline Adventure",description:"Ride ATVs off-road through rugged jungle trails in the Riviera Maya, with options to add ziplines and stop at a cenote along the way."}],hotels:[{name:"Devossion by Live Aqua Playa del Carmen",description:"Adults-only, all-inclusive beachfront resort (formerly the Grand Hyatt Playa del Carmen, rebranded in 2025) on the beach at Calle 26 in downtown Playa del Carmen, a short walk from 5th Avenue and Mamitas Beach. Pools, spa and several à la carte restaurants. Note: guests must be adults (no children), and the all-inclusive dining is not kosher.",price:"$$$$",address:"1a Avenida Esquina Calle 26, Col. Centro, 77710 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+1 800 343 7821",website:"https://www.fiestamericanatravelty.com/en/devossion/hotels/devossion-playa-del-carmen",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d4-grand-hyatt-playa-del-carmen.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Adults-only all-inclusive, so not for families with children. About 1.6 km (roughly a 22-minute walk) from Chabad of Playa del Carmen on 20 Avenida; Hilula kosher bakery is about 1.2 km."},{name:"The Fives Downtown Hotel & Residences, Curio Collection by Hilton",description:"Chic, modern urban residential hotel located on 10th Avenue in 