 del Carmen. Phone +52 984 106 3122. Open Sun–Thu 8 am–11 pm, Fri 8 am–5 pm, Saturday night 7–11 pm."},{name:"Shabbat & holiday meals to go",address:"2 Avenida Benito Juárez, Playa del Carmen",description:"Ready-made meat and parve Shabbat/holiday food to order; WhatsApp +52 984 183 2028 (listed by Chabad)."},{name:"Bend and Levi",address:"Calle 10 Norte Bis, entre Av. 20 y Av. 25, Centro (Hotel 770)"}],transportation:"Taxis operate on fixed union tariffs within town and the Riviera Maya corridor. For travel to Cancun, the ADO Alterna bus terminal runs clean, modern, air-conditioned buses every 10–20 minutes for about MX$124 (ADO quotes vary by departure), taking ~1 hr 5 min to Cancun Central Bus Station. Cozumel passenger ferries depart hourly from the downtown maritime terminal.",travelTips:["Communal Shabbat Atmosphere at Chabad: Chabad of Playa del Carmen hosts legendary Friday night dinners drawing 100+ Jewish travelers from around the globe, with enthusiastic singing, dancing, and abundant multi-course meals. Shabbat day lunch is equally welcoming and hearty.","Public Beach Access by Federal Law: In Playa del Carmen and across Mexico, all ocean beaches are legally public property. Even when beachfront resorts or beach clubs occupy the shoreline, public pedestrian access to and along the sand cannot be restricted or blocked.","Hilula Bakery for Shabbat Provisions: Located on Avenida 20 between Calle 6 and Calle 8, Hilula Bakery is the go-to spot for purchasing fresh Shabbat challah, babka, and baked goods prior to candle lighting.","ADO Alterna Express Bus to Cancun: Skip expensive long-distance taxis and head to the Playa del Carmen Alterna terminal (Av. 20 and Calle 12). Departures to Cancun run every 10 to 20 minutes for about MX$124 (ADO quotes vary by departure). The buses are clean, prompt, and arrive at Cancun Central Bus Station in about 1 hour and 5 minutes.","Excursion Planning on Avenida 5: When booking day excursions (Tulum ruins, cenotes, or the Punta Laguna monkey reserve) from Quinta Avenida kiosks, note that tours can sell out or close early during peak travel seasons and winter breaks. Book well in advance.","Playa del Carmen Taxi Rules & Union Rates: Uber is approved in Quintana Roo, but taxis are still the most common option. The local taxi union sets fixed zone rates. Always agree on the exact total fare with the driver before getting in, especially for trips outside the downtown grid.","Cozumel Ferry Logistics: Passenger ferries to Cozumel depart directly from the downtown maritime terminal by Parque Los Fundadores every hour on the hour. Because two distinct ferry companies (Ultramar and Winjet) alternate hourly departures, buy one-way tickets to keep your return schedule completely flexible.","Cenote Environmental Preservation: All visitors are required to take a cleansing shower before entering natural cenote pools. Chemical sunscreens, bug sprays, and body lotions are strictly prohibited to preserve the sensitive underground Mayan aquifer."],nearby:["Tulum","Cozumel","Akumal","Puerto Morelos"]},{id:"tulum",name:"Tulum",state:"Quintana Roo",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/8aaad048e0bd55d7.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 15m",Miami:"2h 00m",Paris:"10h 40m",London:"9h 55m"},weather:"☀️ 82°F",experiences:["Beaches","National Parks","Volcanoes"],mustDo:"Exploring the Tulum Mayan Ruins overlooking the ocean and biking along the Beach Road",description:"A trendy, boho-chic seaside escape famous for preserved Mayan cliffside ruins, luxurious eco-resorts, yoga retreats, and a warm Jewish community offering Shabbat options.",bestTimeToVisit:"November to December",nearestAirport:"Felipe Carrillo Puerto International Airport (TQO) / Cancún Airport (CUN)",airportDistance:"20 miles from TQO",attractions:[{name:"Tulum Archaeological Site",description:"Ancient Mayan walled city dramatically perched on high limestone cliffs above the sea.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ac4bdb8c49e8aed4.webp"},{name:"Gran Cenote",description:"Famous half-cavern cenote populated by friendly freshwater turtles and small bats."},{name:"Sian Ka’an Biosphere Reserve",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/a36cb59b843f3b13.webp",description:"Massive UNESCO World Heritage site featuring wild dolphins, manatees, and wetlands."}],activities:[{name:"Biking the Beach Road",description:"Rent a beach cruiser to explore chic shops, jungle pathways, and pristine coves."},{name:"Floating down Sian Ka’an Canals",description:"Float gently down crystal-clear freshwater canals constructed by ancient Mayans."}],hotels:[{name:"Dreams Tulum Resort & Spa",description:"Secluded Spanish hacienda-style beachfront resort nestled on an expansive powdery white sand bay north of the Tulum ruins, featuring traditional Mexican arches, palm groves, and quiet oceanfront pools.",price:"$$$",address:"Puerto Juarez, Carretera Chetumal Km. 236, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 871 3333",website:"https://www.hyattinclusivecollection.com/en/resorts-hotels/dreams/mexico/tulum-resort-spa/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/dreams-tulum-resort-spa.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 9 km north of Chabad of Tulum; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Hotel Bardo Tulum",description:"Adults-only mystical jungle sanctuary located in tranquil La Veleta, featuring secluded loft-style villas with private stone plunge pools, lush gardens, outdoor showers, and an ambient firepit lounge.",price:"$$$$",address:"Rio Otate & Rio Basca, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 146 5431",website:"https://www.hotelbardo.mx/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/hotel-bardo-tulum.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 1.5 km (roughly an 18-minute walk) from Chabad of Tulum on Av. Kukulkan in La Veleta."},{name:"Be Tulum (BE DESTINATION Tulum)",description:"Chic barefoot-luxury jungle resort constructed with native stone, reclaimed wood, and limestone on Tulum’s south beach road, featuring rooftop plunge pools and oceanfront daybeds.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Carretera Tulum-Boca Paila Km 10, Zona Hotelera, 77780 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 980 0678",website:"https://www.betulum.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/be-tulum-hotel-tulum.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 7.5 km from Chabad of Tulum via the beach road; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"La Valise Tulum",description:"Exclusive 11-room boutique beachfront sanctuary famous for handcrafted artisan suites with open-air master beds that roll out onto private oceanfront terraces overlooking the Caribbean.",price:"$$$$",address:"Carr. Tulum-Boca Paila Km 8.7, Tulum Beach, Zona Hotelera, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 55 3439 1161",website:"https://lavalisetulum.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/la-valise-tulum-tulum.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 7 km from Chabad of Tulum; not walkable for Shabbat."}],restaurants:[{name:"Chabad Tulum Kosher Kitchen",description:"Glatt kosher home-style catering, fresh pita, falafel, and communal Shabbat dinners (note: operating hours and daily menu availability fluctuate seasonally with tourist traffic; lower confidence on fixed off-season daily hours, please verify in advance).",kosher:!0}],transportation:"Bicycles are the primary, most scenic way to traverse the Beach Road. Car rentals are helpful for long distance.",nearby:["Coba Ruins","Akumal","Muyil Ruins"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of Tulum",address:"Villa Flor De Mayo, Av. Kukulkan Manzana 57 Lote 3, La Veleta, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Netanel Binyamini",phone:"+52 984 246 1111",website:"https://chabadtulum.org",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Chabad Tulum Kosher Kitchen",photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",address:"Villa Flor De Mayo, Av. Kukulkan Mz 57 Lt 3, La Veleta, Tulum",kashrus:"Chabad of Tulum (Glatt Kosher)",phone:"+52 984 246 1111",website:"https://chabadtulum.org",type:"Grill / Shabbat Catering / Mexican Kosher"},{name:"Café Mor Tulum",address:"Chabad Tulum, Av. Kukulkan Mz 57 Lt 3 (Villa Flor de Mayo), La Veleta, Tulum",kashrus:"Kosher dairy (Chabad Tulum's café, as Chabad Tulum states it)",phone:"+52 984 246 1111",website:"https://chabadtulum.org/cafemor",type:"Dairy café & bakery",description:"Kosher dairy bakery and kitchen: pastries, bagels and breakfast; Sun–Fri 8 am–4 pm (per its Instagram)."}]},{id:"cabo-san-lucas",businessesAndServicesList:[{name:"The Cabo Mikva (Cabo Jewish Center)",category:"Mikvah",address:"Camino de la Plaza 135, Cabo S Lucas, Baja California Sur 23450",phone:"+52-624-186-4602",website:"https://www.jewishcabo.org/",description:"Women's mikvah at the Cabo Jewish Center (Chabad); by appointment; center phone +52-624-133-0489"}],mikvah:{name:"The Cabo Mikva (Cabo Jewish Center)",address:"Camino de la Plaza 135, Cabo S Lucas, Baja California Sur 23450"},name:"Cabo San Lucas",state:"Baja California Sur",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ff99b06e4d625519.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"5h 45m",Miami:"4h 30m",Paris:"12h 00m",London:"11h 15m"},weather:"☀️ 82°F",experiences:["Beaches","Whale Watching","Off-Road Adventures"],mustDo:"Taking a boat tour to El Arco (The Arch) and whale watching in the Sea of Cortez",description:"A spectacular desert-meets-ocean destination at the southern tip of the Baja Peninsula, offering dramatic rock formations, luxury golf resorts, and an active Chabad catering to Jewish tourists.",bestTimeToVisit:"May to June",nearestAirport:"Los Cabos International Airport (SJD)",airportDistance:"28 miles",attractions:[{name:"El Arco & Land’s End (The Arch of Cabo San Lucas)",description:"Iconic granite archway standing 200 feet tall where the Sea of Cortez meets the Pacific Ocean, best experienced via glass-bottom boat tour."},{name:"Playa del Amor (Lover’s Beach) & Pelican Rock",description:"Secluded beach nestled between towering granite cliffs, accessible only by water taxi or boat, popular for snorkeling and swimming."},{name:"Playa El Médano (Medano Beach)",description:"Cabo's main safe-swimming beach, known for gentle waves, water sports like paddleboarding, and beachfront views toward El Arco.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d-playa-el-m-dano-medano-beach.webp"},{name:"Chileno Bay & Santa Maria Beach",description:"Chileno Bay and Santa Maria Beach are two Blue Flag beaches on the Tourist Corridor near Cabo San Lucas. Both bays are sheltered from strong waves, with calm, clear water popular for swimming and snorkeling. Chileno Bay has showers and restrooms."},{name:"Marina Cabo San Lucas Boardwalk",description:"Yacht harbor and marina in Cabo San Lucas with a pedestrian boardwalk lined with shops, restaurants, and sunset tour boats."},{name:"Mount Solmar & Cerro del Vigía",description:"Dramatic granite peak above Land’s End offering an exhilarating desert ridge hike with 360-degree ocean panoramas."},{name:"Mercado Orgánico San José & Mercado Popular",description:"Organic market in San José del Cabo (at Club La Huerta) with local crafts, produce, food stalls, and handmade goods, held on Saturdays."},{name:"Cabo Pulmo National Marine Park",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/51f8499c40fe70ee.webp",description:"Day trip · about 95 km from Cabo San Lucas. National marine park on the east coast of the Baja California Peninsula. It protects the northernmost coral reef in the eastern Pacific, estimated at about 20,000 years old. Known for snorkeling and diving."}],activities:[{name:"Glass-Bottom Boat Tour to El Arco & Land’s End",description:"Glide across crystal turquoise waters viewing marine life directly through glass hulls past sea lion colonies and dramatic granite spires."},{name:"Seasonal Humpback & Gray Whale Watching",description:"Encounter wild migrating whales breaching and singing in the Sea of Cortez and Pacific Ocean (Dec 15 – Apr 15)."},{name:"Wild Canyon Desert Adventures (ATVs & Ziplines)",description:"Race quads through rugged desert canyons and zip-line hundreds of feet above deep chasms on monster canyon lines."},{name:"Pelican Rock Water Sports & Scuba Diving",description:"Pelican Rock is a snorkeling and dive site off Cabo San Lucas in calm, clear Sea of Cortez water, a short boat ride from the marina. It starts as a small reef suitable for beginners, with rock formations, tropical fish and sea lions."},{name:"Deep-Sea Sportfishing Charters",description:"Depart from the marina to legendary offshore ocean banks targeting striped marlin, dorado, yellowfin tuna, and wahoo."},{name:"Luxury Desert Oceanfront Spa Experiences",description:"Spa experiences in the Cabo San Lucas area offering botanical treatments and oceanfront or garden settings."}],travelTips:["Pacific Ocean vs. Sea of Cortez Swimmability: Most open Pacific-facing beaches in Cabo have treacherous shorebreaks and severe undertows where swimming is strictly prohibited. Stick to designated swimmable beaches like Playa El Médano, Chileno Bay, and Santa Maria Beach.","Whale Watching Timing: Peak humpback and gray whale migration occurs between mid-December and mid-April. Early morning boat departures (8:00 AM–9:30 AM) offer the calmest sea surface and easiest whale spotting.","Kosher Meal Pre-Coordination Rule: Resort kosher dining is strictly NOT available on-demand at check-in. Coordinate with Rabbi Benny at Chabad of Cabo San Lucas at least 1–2 weeks prior to arrival to schedule catering and a mashgiach.","Corridor Transportation: The Tourist Corridor between Cabo San Lucas and San José del Cabo spans 20 miles. Rental cars or pre-arranged private transfers are far more cost-effective than relying on individual hotel taxi dispatches, which have steep flat union rates.","Shabbat Logistics in Los Cabos: Chabad is located in the Pedregal district of Cabo San Lucas. If staying out along the corridor (e.g. Solaz or Zadún), arrange Shabbat delivery boxes in advance as walking to shul from the corridor is not feasible."],hotels:[{name:"Waldorf Astoria Los Cabos Pedregal",description:"Spectacular 5-star ultra-luxury resort carved into towering granite cliffs at Land’s End, entered through a private torch-lit chandelier tunnel piercing the mountain. Every room features a private plunge pool, panoramic Pacific ocean views, and personal concierge service. The premier choice for Shabbat travelers due to its walking proximity to Chabad.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Cam. del Mar 1, Pedregal, 23455 Cabo San Lucas, B.C.S., Mexico",phone:"+52 624 163 4300",website:"https://www.waldorfastorialoscabospedregal.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/waldorf-astoria-los-cabos-pedregal-cabo-san-lucas.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.75 km (roughly a 10-minute walk by map routing) from the Cabo Jewish Center / Chabad of Cabo at Camino de la Plaza 135, Pedregal."},{name:"Zadún, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve",description:"Ultra-luxurious coastal sanctuary set where dramatic desert bluffs meet the Sea of Cortez, offering breathtaking desert-meets-ocean scenery. Standalone ocean-view pavilions each feature a private plunge pool and dedicated Tosoani private butler. Seasonal whale watching is frequently visible directly from private room terraces.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Blvd. Mar de Cortez, 23403 San José del Cabo, B.C.S., Mexico",phone:"+52 624 172 9000",website:"https://www.ritzcarlton.com/en/hotels/sjdzr-zadun-a-ritz-carlton-reserve/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/zadun-a-ritz-carlton-reserve-cabo-san-lucas.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Beyond Kosher Experience: separate meat and dairy kitchens supervised by Chabad of Cabo (K-abo Kosher), glatt meat, cholov Yisroel dairy, Shabbat menu. Mashgiach fee $200/day paid to Chabad; book at least 72 hours ahead. About 34 km from Cabo San Lucas."},{name:"Solaz, a Luxury Collection Resort, Los Cabos",description:"Contemporary architectural resort along the Tourist Corridor featuring an on-site certified kosher culinary program, cascading infinity pools, private ocean terraces, and multi-bedroom residences and suites with full kitchens and kitchenettes.",price:"$$$$",address:"KM 18.5 Carretera Transpeninsular CSL-SJC, Tourist Corridor, 23405 San José del Cabo, B.C.S., Mexico",phone:"+52 624 144 2100",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/sjdlc-solaz-a-luxury-collection-resort-los-cabos/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/solaz-los-cabos.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"On-site kosher program: breakfast at Cascabel, dairy lunch at Riccio di Mare, meat dinner at Mako, plus Shabbat meals. For Shabbat, room motion sensors (lights, A/C) and the electronic door lock can be turned off on request."}],restaurants:[{name:"Cabo Jewish Center kosher catering / Shabbat takeout",description:"Fresh, gourmet Glatt Kosher Mexican dishes, steaks, fish, and Shabbat takeout cooked fresh under Rabbi Hershcovich.",kosher:!0}],transportation:"Taxis are reliable but expensive. Car rentals are highly recommended to explore nearby San Jose del Cabo.",nearby:["San Jose del Cabo","Todos Santos","Cabo Pulmo"],chabad:[{name:"Cabo Jewish Center / Chabad of Cabo",address:"Cam. de La Pl. 135, Pedregal, 23450 Cabo San Lucas, B.C.S., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Benzion (Benny) Hershcovich",phone:"+52 624 133 0489",website:"http://www.jewishcabo.org",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/cabo-jewish-center-chabad-of-cabo-cabo-san-lucas.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Ray's Cabo Kosher (at Cabo Jewish Center)",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/cabo-kosher-chabad-center.webp",address:"Cam. de La Pl. 135, Pedregal, Cabo San Lucas",kashrus:"Rabbi Benny Hershcovich, Chabad of Cabo",phone:"+52 624 125 7932",website:"https://www.jewishcabo.org/kosher",type:"