ill (kosher, Polanco) and 3 km from Chabad Lubavitch at Calderón de la Barca 339."}],restaurants:[{name:"Auguri Kosher Trattoria",description:"Top-rated kosher dining experience in Mexico City! Exceptional Italian trattoria serving pasta, risotto, and fish, featuring two dedicated sub-menus: Kosher Bamboo (Asian stir-fries & sushi) and Burger House (gourmet burgers & sandwiches).",kosher:!0},{name:"Gaucho Grill Polanco Kosher",description:"Renowned Glatt Kosher Argentinian steakhouse offering prime cuts, charcoal grill delicacies, empanadas, and warm soft-shell corn tortillas served in warming cloth pouches under KMD supervision.",kosher:!0},{name:"Pecorino Kosher",description:"Bustling, high-energy Chalav Yisrael Italian trattoria in Polanco serving artisanal wood-fired pizzas, handcrafted pastas, and fresh salads under KMD oversight.",kosher:!0},{name:"Sinai Deli & Bakery",description:"Classic Polanco kosher deli and bakery serving hearty breakfast platters, omelets, fresh pastries, and European baked goods under KMD.",kosher:!0},{name:"Ajla Gourmet Polanco",description:"Chic gourmet kosher breakfast spot and artisanal bakery in Polanco known for superb coffees, morning plates, and fresh baked breads.",kosher:!0},{name:"Wendy's Kosher Bakery",description:"Premier KMD-certified kosher bakery in Polanco featuring fresh Shabbat challot, babkas, pastries, and artisanal breads.",kosher:!0}],transportation:"DiDi has a very large presence in Mexico City and is often cheaper than Uber. Rush hours are roughly 6–10 AM, 1–3 PM (school traffic) and 6–9 PM. Always use licensed ride-hailing apps rather than hailing street cabs.",travelTips:["Rideshare App Comparison (DiDi vs Uber): Download DiDi before arriving in Mexico City. DiDi has extensive driver availability and is routinely 30–40% cheaper than Uber. If a DiDi driver’s final fare increases after the trip, tap the help button in the app to request an immediate refund back to the initial quote.","High-Altitude Dry Climate & Lip Care: Mexico City sits at an elevation of 7,350 feet (2,240m). The mountain air is notably dry and combined with urban smog can cause dry, chapped, or swollen lips. Keep ChapStick/lip balm on hand and drink plenty of bottled water (tap water is not potable).","Safety & Visible Police Presence: Mexico City maintains a heavy, reassuring tourist police presence across Polanco, Reforma, Centro Histórico, Roma, and Condesa. Daytime and early evening walking along main avenues is comfortable and safe.","MEX Airport Terminal 2 Departures: Arrive at least 2 hours before domestic flights.","Chapultepec Castle & Park Logistics: Chapultepec Castle is North America’s only royal-inhabited castle (Emperor Maximilian I and Empress Carlota). Note that public restrooms within the surrounding Bosque de Chapultepec park charge a small cash entry fee (~MX$5 coins required). The uphill walk takes 10–15 minutes.","Xochimilco Canal Booking at Embarcadero Nativitas: Head to Embarcadero Nuevo Nativitas (the largest dock). Trajinera boat rentals have an official rate set by the Xochimilco borough of MX$750 per hour for the whole boat (2025), not per person. Confirm duration and price before boarding.","KMD Kosher Certification: The main kosher certifier in Mexico City is KMD (Kashrut Maguen David), Horacio 1008, Polanco. Check kosher.com.mx for current certified products and establishments."],nearby:["Coyoacán","Puebla","Lomas de Chapultepec"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad CDMX - Polanco",address:"C. Calderón de la Barca 339, Polanco, Polanco III Secc, Miguel Hidalgo, 11550 Ciudad de México, CDMX, Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Mayzlesh",phone:"+52 55 5545 6770",website:"http://chabadofmexico.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"},{name:"Chabad of Bosques",address:"Av. de los Bosques 50, Estado de Mexico, 53950 Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Yosef Y Mayzlesh; Mrs. Tova Mayzlesh; Rabbi Sholom Dov Ber Mayzlesh; Mrs. Rivkah Mayzlesh",phone:"52-55-5989-0770",notes:"Bosques de las Lomas, west Mexic